' The body of operator-api-request.puml / operator-api-request-dark.puml. Not a
' diagram on its own: it carries no start marker, so PlantUML will not render
' this file directly.
'
' Careful: the start and end markers must not appear in this file *at all*, not
' even inside a comment like this one. PlantUML scans for them lexically, so a
' comment that merely names one opens a second diagram here and the include
' fails with a line number pointing at neither.
'
' Split out because OPERATOR-API.md embeds a light and a dark render and they
' must not drift. Everything the same in both lives here; each wrapper adds only
' the colours that differ. See README.md for why a global flag cannot do this.

' A post-render step widens this single font name into a fallback stack, so a
' viewer without Inter gets a sans-serif rather than the monospace a missing
' font can otherwise fall back to.
skinparam defaultFontName Inter
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

title One operator request: identify, authorise, record, then act

header
Every handler does the same four steps in the same order.
The <b>record precedes the action</b>: one written afterwards can be missing for something that happened.
Rationale: <b>ARCHITECTURE.md</b> S3.   Endpoints and payloads: <b>OPERATOR-API.md</b>.
endheader

actor "admin client\ncurl · panel · bot" as client $c_client
participant "**operator-api**\naxum, one process" as api $c_api
participant "**Authenticator**  «Strategy»\ntoken · mtls · oidc · jwt\nlive: rebuilt when the TOML changes" as auth $c_auth
database "**audit file**\nappend-only JSONL\nflushed per record" as file $c_file
participant "**the service**\nuserdata · metadata · permissions\nmoderation · text · audit · health\nserver-config · session-*" as svc $c_svc

client -> api : HTTP + Authorization

api -> auth : identify(header)
alt no credential, or not this mode's shape
  auth --> api : Missing | Malformed
  api --> client : **401** {"error": ...}
else genuine but not accepted here, or no mapped scope
  auth --> api : Rejected | Unscoped
  api --> client : **403**
else identified
  auth --> api : Identity {subject, scopes}
  note right of auth $c_auth
    The subject is the <b>variable name</b>, never the token value:
    token:STARLING_ADMIN_TOKEN. An audit record must not contain
    the credential whose use it records.
  end note

  api -> api : identity.allows(scope)?
  alt lacks the scope this route needs
    api --> client : **403** this identity does not hold X
  else
    api -> file : {id, at_ms, subject, action, outcome:"accepted"}
    alt the write failed and audit.fail_closed
      file --> api : io error
      api --> client : **503** not recorded, so it did not happen
    else recorded, or fail_closed = false
      api -> svc : gRPC, carrying Actor{Operator{subject, scope}}
      note right of api $c_svc
        <b>Not a second policy implementation.</b> The same methods the
        gateway calls, with an operator identity instead of a session.
        The Actor is not authorisation, the services trust this plane,
        it is so the change has a name against it in the service's log.
      end note
      alt unreachable, or a transport error
        svc --> api : tonic::Status
        api --> client : **502** <service> is unreachable
      else applied = false
        svc --> api : {applied: false, refused: "..."}
        api --> client : **409**, or **404** when the target is gone
      else applied
        svc --> api : the result
        api --> client : **200** body, or **204**
      end
    end
  end
end

legend bottom
  <b>Why 401 and 403 stay apart.</b>  401 is "who are you", 403 is "not you",
  and they send an operator to different files. Collapsing them was a bug.
  --
  <b>Why the record is fail-closed.</b>  audit is an optional service, and the
  highest-privilege plane must not depend on one an operator may not run, so
  this file is written by this process. fail_closed = false trades the refusal
  for a logged error: the operator's decision, and not the default.
endlegend
